WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:06.029
Syria's war is mess.

00:00:06.029 --> 00:00:09.380
After 6 years, the conflict is divided between
four sides,

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.820
each side with foreign backers.

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:15.940
And those foreign backers don't even agree
with each other on who they are fighting for

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.699
and who they are fighting against.

00:00:17.699 --> 00:00:22.680
And now, Syria’s use of chemical weapons has
provoked President Donald Trump to directly

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.100
attack Syrian President Bashar al-Assad.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.500
This is a major development, because, up until now,

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.609
the US has only been focused on fighting ISIS.

00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:34.870
To understand the criss-crossing interventions
and battle lines in Syria today, and how it

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.840
got this way, it helps to go back to the beginning of the conflict

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.859
and watch to see how it unfolded.

00:00:40.859 --> 00:00:46.149
The first shots in the war were fired, in March
2011, by Syrian dictator Bashar al-Assad against

00:00:46.149 --> 00:00:48.060
peaceful Arab Spring demonstrators.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.359
In July the protesters

00:00:54.359 --> 00:00:55.440
start shooting back,

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.149
and some Syrian troops
even defect from the Syrian army to join them.

00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:03.380
They call themselves the Free Syrian Army
and the uprising becomes a civil war.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:09.820
Extremists from around the region and the world start traveling to Syria to join the rebels.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:14.259
Now, Assad actually encourages this by releasing
jihadist prisoners to tinge the rebellion

00:01:14.259 --> 00:01:17.960
with extremism and make it harder for foreign
backers to support them.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:23.360
In January 2012, al-Qaeda forms a new branch
in Syria, Jabhat al-Nusra.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:27.900
Also around that time, Syrian Kurdish groups, who
had long sought autonomy,

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:29.040
take up arms and

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:32.469
informally secede from Assad's rule in the
north.

00:01:32.469 --> 00:01:35.320
That summer is when Syria becomes a proxy
war.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:39.359
Iran, Assad's most important ally, intervenes
on his behalf.

00:01:39.359 --> 00:01:44.460
By the end of 2012, Iran is sending daily
cargo flights and has hundreds of officers

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:45.460
on the ground.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:49.420
At the same time, the oil-rich Arab states
on the Persian Gulf begin sending money and

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:53.040
weapons to the rebels, mainly to counter Iran’s
influence.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:57.480
Iran steps up its influence in turn,

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:02.299
in mid-2012 when Hezbollah,
 a Lebanese militia backed by Iran,

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.140
invades to fight along Assad.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:06.780
In turn the Gulf States respond,

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:09.000
Saudi Arabia really stepping up this time,

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.640
to send more money and weapons

00:02:10.649 --> 00:02:11.500
to the rebels,

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.060
This time through Jordan who
also opposes Assad.

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:18.080
By 2013, the Middle East is divided between

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:21.260
mostly Sunni powers, generally supporting the rebels,

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.980
and Shias, generally supporting Assad.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.140
That April, the Obama administration,

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:30.580
horrified by Assad's atrocities and the mounting death toll,

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:35.460
signs a secret order authorizing the
CIA to train and equip Syrian rebels.

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:36.750
But the program stalls.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:42.489
At the same time, the US quietly urges Arab
Gulf states to stop funding extremists, but

00:02:42.489 --> 00:02:44.629
their requests basically go ignored.

00:02:44.629 --> 00:02:49.920
In August, the Assad regime uses chemical weapons, provoking condemnation around the world

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:54.720
Obama: "Men, women, and children lying in

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:56.709
rows – killed by poison gas..."

00:02:56.709 --> 00:03:02.340
It is in the national security interests of
the United States to respond to the Assad

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:06.260
regime's use of chemical weapons
through a targeted military strike.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:12.200
Russia proposed on Monday that Syria surrender
control over its chemical weapons to the international

00:03:12.209 --> 00:03:15.140
community for its eventual dismantling, to avoid a US

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:16.460
military strike.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:19.769
The US ends up backing down, but the whole thing establishes Syria as

00:03:19.769 --> 00:03:25.599
a great-powers dispute, with Russia backing Assad and the US opposing him.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:31.120
Just weeks later, the first American CIA training
and arms reach Syrian rebels.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.740
The US is now a participant in the war.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:39.000
In February 2014, something happens that transforms
the war:

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.540
an al-Qaeda affiliate, based mostly

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:45.680
in Iraq, breaks away from the group over internal
disagreements.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:51.160
The group calls itself the Islamic State of
Iraq and Syria, or ISIS,

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.160
and it becomes al-Qaeda's enemy.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:59.040
ISIS mostly fights not Assad, but other
rebels and Kurds, carving out a mini-state

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.500
it calls its Caliphate.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:06.340
That summer, it marches across Iraq seizing
territory, galvanizing the world against it.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:12.220
In September, one year after the US almost
bombed Assad, it begins bombing ISIS.

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:15.000
Obama: “We're moving ahead with our campaign
of airstrikes against these terrorists,

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.760
and we're prepared to take action against
ISIL in Syria as well.”

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:24.940
That summer, in July, the Pentagon launches
its own program to train Syrian rebels —

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:28.360
but will only those who'll fight ISIS, not Assad.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:34.010
The program fizzles, showing that America
now opposes ISIS more than Assad, but that there's also

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:38.950
no like-minded Syrian proxy forces on the ground in Syria.

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:43.400
In August, Turkey starts bombing Kurdish groups in
Iraq and in Turkey,

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:46.080
even as these Kurdish groups are fight

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.910
ISIS in Syria. But Turkey doesn't bomb ISIS.

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:51.560
This gets to one of the big problems in this conflict:

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.890
the US sees ISIS
as its main enemy, but the US’ allies like

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:59.420
Turkey and a lot of other Middle Eastern states have
other priorities.

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:02.460
This makes for a lot of unclear and confusing alliances.

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:10.360
The next month, in September, Russia intervenes
on behalf of Assad, sending a few dozen military

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:13.920
aircraft to a long-held Russian base in the
country.

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:15.660
Russia says it's there to bomb ISIS,

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.440
but in fact only ends up bombing

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.510
anti-Assad rebels, including some

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:20.680
backed by the US.

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:24.280
The next year, Donald Trump wins the White
House,

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:27.250
vowing to stay out of Syria, and signaling

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:29.740
that Assad should be able to stay in power.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:36.580
At the end of 2016, Assad, helped by Russian
airpower and Iranian sponsored militias, retakes

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.180
the Syrian city of Aleppo,

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:42.790
knocking the rebels
out of their last remaining urban stronghold.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:49.120
Then, in Spring 2017, Assad once again
uses chemical weapons against his people,

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:52.030
killing 85, including 20 children.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:58.350
Back in the US, Trump says his attitude toward
Syria and Assad has “changed very much”

00:05:58.350 --> 00:05:59.350
due to the attacks.

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:00.440
He vows to respond

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:07.430
and within days the White House launches dozens
of tomahawk missiles that strike an airbase in Syria.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:12.450
This is the first time the United States has directly attacked the Assad regime.

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:17.320
This adds yet another criss crossing complication
to an already multidimensional civil war.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:21.040
So as it stands now, Syria is in ruins.

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:24.270
Even as Assad recaptures land, the rebellion
perseveres.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:29.210
And with outside countries fueling each of
the groups, it’s clear that there is still

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:30.620
no end in sight.

